KG42.register("clusters-c215663bc7f805c146388363",{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v142-d-K003","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","label":"Consumption updates, uniform pricing, and payment interfaces in the price-expectation game","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Consumption updates, uniform pricing, and payment interfaces in the price-expectation game","market_meaning":"In the described myopic best-response computation, a user sends updates to other users when changing consumption; the energy provider forms a uniform time-period price based on the given consumption state, and the user bears charges according to their own consumption quantity and that price. The existing chains cover the communication and pricing-settlement interfaces but do not yet form a complete best-response or equilibrium-allocation rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R008 and R009 define price and payment for a given consumption state, while R007 applies only to the myopic best-response algorithm used in the text to compute Nash equilibrium. Communication updates and pricing share the game consumption state, but the source does not specify that each message triggers immediate repricing by the provider, nor does it provide convergence conditions usable in this cluster.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The consumption choice affects both the uniform price and the individual payment; the consumption-update message serves the response computation of the same game; and the three chains form a conditional interface for communication, pricing and obligation. Upstream omissions concerning the complete strategic decision and equilibrium conditions are retained as gaps.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the inter-user message obligation triggered by consumption changes within the described equilibrium-computation algorithm, limited to that implementation scenario."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the rule from aggregate consumption to the uniform time-period price and the scope of price-expectation behavior."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the obligation that the uniform price and individual consumption jointly determine the time-period payment."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-N01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-n-k","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e02-price-anticipator-game","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27"],"rationale":"The message content is a consumption update in the same price-expectation game, and the pricing rule takes the consumption state as input; here only the complementary scope of algorithmic communication and pricing is connected, without asserting that messages are passed to the provider or that each message triggers price recalculation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-N02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-n-k","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-p-k","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n-k","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-p-k","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"],"rationale":"The same consumption state forms a uniform price through the same price function, and that price then jointly determines the time-period charge with the user's own consumption quantity. The price is retained as a function of consumption and is not replaced by a fixed-price parameter."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-n-k","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n-k"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27"],"rationale":"Under the same user, time period and game state, the two refer to the same consumption component and respectively take the local roles of aggregate-pricing input and individual-payment multiplier."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-p-k","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-p-k"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"],"rationale":"Both are the aggregate-consumption price function for the same time period in M03, used respectively for price formation and charge calculation; the local definitions and the still-missing unit information are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O03","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"],"rationale":"Within the same consumption state and price-expectation scope, the two describe the same time-period payment obligation respectively in procedural text and mathematical expression; the association is retained and they are not counted as two independent payment rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The B candidate citation contains the benefit function and Nash-equilibrium conditions, but R007-R009 do not incorporate them into the frozen chains; R007 also does not provide the complete best-response update, execution order, or stopping or convergence conditions. Therefore, the communication and pricing-payment interfaces cannot yet be closed into an equilibrium-computation rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g03-e02-price-anticipator-game"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream is to supplement the M03 benefit and equilibrium conditions and the original applicable premises, and to verify the execution and termination basis required by the best-response algorithm; content not provided by the source remains blank, and convergence or welfare optimality is not derived from the message account."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The consumption strategy is bound only to an abstract feasible set, and the current M03 citation does not give precise time-period boundaries; the units of consumption quantity and the price function have also not been confirmed. The existing C2 revision request for R009 has not yet been resolved, and it cannot be directly filled from same-named symbols in M02.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-n-k","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-p-k","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n-k","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-p-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the feasible-set definition, time-period measurement and price-function units applicable to M03, provide same-mechanism source bindings, and implement the R009 revision request."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Existing declaration and price-coordination nodes do not fully express inter-user consumption updates, myopic best-response computation and strategic Nash equilibrium; the related proposals have still not been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g03-e02-price-anticipator-game"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P02","proposal:v141-b-g03-peer-message-best-response"],"required_work":"Manually check the equilibrium and inter-user communication node proposals, distinguishing the semantics of consumption declaration, state update and strategic decision; this round does not insert new nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The citations in this cluster for pricing, payment, game strategy and algorithmic communication all remain unverified; the current mappings are only experimental candidate assemblies and have not undergone independent source or scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g03-e02-price-anticipator-game"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the citations and their algorithm scope, consumption-state interface and payment expressions, and retain the current unaudited source status."}]},"rule_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R007","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R008","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-4713ffee78f85526","COMP-a88f30097237f433","COMP-bb0098757e6823b6"]});
